---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
// TODO: replace href="#" with Amazon Associates links (OneLink) once account approved.
// Four picks as of 2026-07-30 (Antonio's ruling): added the official
// AlphaTheta x SanDisk DJ Flash Drive (real partnership, announced May 2025,
// sold via pioneerdjstore.com/products/sandisk-dj-flash-drive -- source:
// alphatheta.com + pioneerdj.com news) and the Kingston DataTraveler, the
// budget name that keeps coming up on Pioneer's own community forum
// alongside SanDisk Extreme Pro. Not an affiliate link (no Pioneer/SanDisk
// program), so it stays plain rel="noopener", no "sponsored".
---
<Base
  title="The DJ Emergency Kit - USB Drives That Don't Die | Save My Gig!"
  description="The USB drives worth trusting with your gig, shortlisted from DJ forums, user reports and hardware databases. Four per category, no filler."
  path="/gear"
>
  <main class="wrap">
    <div class="status-line">Approved_Gear</div>

    <h1 style="margin-bottom:1rem">THE EMERGENCY <span class="accent">KIT</span></h1>
    {/* HONESTY CORRECTION (Antonio, 2026-08-03). This said "What I actually
        carry", and the meta description said "chosen after 35 years around DJ
        booths". Both are personal-experience claims the project cannot back.
        Flow principle 8: every recommendation is backed by official
        documentation or repeated real-world evidence, and if we do not know,
        we do not guess. The shortlist is real; its basis is RESEARCH, so that
        is what it says now.
        DELIBERATELY SILENT ON AFFILIATION. The links already carry
        rel="sponsored" and an affiliate_click event, so printing "no
        affiliate deals" would become false the day a tag is added. Say where
        the picks came from, not how they are paid for. */}
    <p class="dim" style="margin-bottom:1rem">We have not carried every drive on this page, and we are not going to pretend otherwise. This shortlist is research: DJ forums, communities, user reports and hardware databases, filtered down to four per category, because a wall of links means nobody chose anything. One drive here is certified by AlphaTheta. The other three are the ones working DJs keep coming back to.</p>

    <div class="panel">
      <h2 style="margin-bottom:0.5rem">Main USB drives</h2>
      <p class="dim">32-64 GB is the sweet spot: big enough for a full working library, small enough that FAT32 formats without drama.</p>
      <p class="dim" style="font-size:0.85rem">Some links on this page may earn us a commission at no extra cost to you. It never changes what we recommend, and there are no paid links inside Emergency Mode.</p>
      <div class="grid grid-2">
        <div class="card">
          <h3 style="font-size:1rem">SanDisk Extreme Pro USB 3.2</h3>
          <p>Metal body, fast, survives years of booth abuse. The default answer.</p>
          <a href="https://www.amazon.com/s?k=SanDisk+Extreme+Pro+USB+3.2+Flash+Drive" target="_blank" rel="noopener sponsored" class="btn btn-neutral" data-event="affiliate_click" data-program="amazon" data-placement="gear_main_1">Check price →</a>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <h3 style="font-size:1rem">SanDisk DJ Flash Drive</h3>
          <p>The official AlphaTheta x SanDisk drive. Bigger than one set needs (512GB or 1TB) but ships FAT32-ready and doubles as your archive, not just your export stick.</p>
          <a href="https://pioneerdjstore.com/products/sandisk-dj-flash-drive" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="btn btn-neutral" data-event="affiliate_click" data-program="pioneerdjstore" data-placement="gear_main_3">Check price →</a>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <h3 style="font-size:1rem">Samsung BAR Plus</h3>
          <p>Solid metal unibody, no cap to lose, quietly reliable.</p>
          <a href="https://www.amazon.com/s?k=Samsung+BAR+Plus+USB+Flash+Drive" target="_blank" rel="noopener sponsored" class="btn btn-neutral" data-event="affiliate_click" data-program="amazon" data-placement="gear_main_2">Check price →</a>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <h3 style="font-size:1rem">Kingston DataTraveler 32GB USB3</h3>
          <p>The budget pick DJs still vouch for. Reliable once formatted to FAT32. A quick format is fine on a drive you trust; full-format one you suspect, because that doubles as a stress test.</p>
          <a href="https://www.amazon.com/s?k=Kingston+DataTraveler+32GB+USB+3.0" target="_blank" rel="noopener sponsored" class="btn btn-neutral" data-event="affiliate_click" data-program="amazon" data-placement="gear_main_4">Check price →</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="panel">
      <h3 style="margin-bottom:0.5rem">The backup that lives in your pocket</h3>
      <p class="dim" style="margin-bottom:0">Buy two of whichever main drive you pick. Identical drives, identical exports. That's the whole trick, redundancy beats recovery every time.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="panel">
      <h3 style="margin-bottom:0.5rem">Worth adding</h3>
      <ul class="checklist">
        <li>A small hard case or keyring capsule, crushed and wet drives are the classic lab jobs.</li>
        <li>A USB-C ↔ USB-A adapter, the booth laptop never has the port you need.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <p class="dim" style="margin-top:2rem">
      Drive already failed? <a href="/recovery">Recovery route →</a> ·
      Full prevention system: <a href="/prepare">Never again →</a>
    </p>
  </main>
</Base>
